From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: clear stale GL errors before multisample caps query

On some drivers (particularly Mali/Panthor with Mesa), capability
detection may leave stale GL errors. The assertion in
vrend_renderer_query_multisample_caps() was crashing virgl_render_server
on ARM64 platforms with the message:
"Stale error state detected, please check for failures in initialization"

Replace the assertion with a loop that clears any stale errors and logs
a warning, allowing the render server to continue functioning.

BUG=b:chromium:XXXXXX
TEST=Verified VM starts successfully on RK3588 with Mali-G610

Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_formats.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c b/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c
@@ -706,6 +706,7 @@ unsigned vrend_renderer_query_multisample_caps(unsigned max_samples, struct virg
 {
    GLuint tex;
    GLuint fbo;
+   GLenum err;
    GLenum status;

    unsigned max_samples_confirmed = 1;
@@ -713,8 +714,12 @@ unsigned vrend_renderer_query_multisample_caps(unsigned max_samples, struct virg
    int out_buf_offsets[4] = {0,1,2,4};
    int lowest_working_ms_count_idx = -1;

-   assert(glGetError() == GL_NO_ERROR &&
-          "Stale error state detected, please check for failures in initialization");
+   /* Clear any stale GL errors from previous operations (e.g., capability
+    * detection). Some drivers may leave errors that don't affect functionality.
+    */
+   while ((err = glGetError()) != GL_NO_ERROR) {
+      virgl_warn("Stale GL error 0x%x detected before multisample caps query\n", err);
+   }

    glGenFramebuffers( 1, &fbo );
    memset(caps->sample_locations, 0, 8 * sizeof(uint32_t));
--
